{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia","id":1211787,"title":"Essence-Equivalent for Goetia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-26T07:17:39-07:00","id":1211787,"title":"Essence-Equivalent for Goetia","content":"Hello, everyone! I've been thinking a bit about the different &quot;fuel&quot; out there, and I kind of like the idea of having separate types. So spirits run on Essence, faeries on Glamour, I make ghosts run on Plasm, and then for goetia... I've no idea. I can't think of a good name for goetia-fuel, at all, so I was wondering if anyone has any idea for what to call it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, and if anyone has suggestions for something else to call goetia, too, that would be great. It's not a bad name, but it's got too specific connotations for me to want to use it for all sorts of astral entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24057-malus-black","name":"Malus Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:40:58-07:00","id":1211794,"title":"","content":"Beast Player's Guide refers to Goetia as Dreamborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:04:45-07:00","id":1211807,"title":"","content":"I would call it : &quot;Malice&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:10:35-07:00","id":1211811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lykas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1211807#post1211807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would call it : &amp;quot;Malice&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Even for non-malicious Goetia/Dreamborn, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:19:18-07:00","id":1211813,"title":"","content":"How about <a href=\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/ken\" target=\"_blank\">Ken</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-26-2018, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:20:20-07:00","id":1211814,"title":"","content":"I would go with Qualia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:28:27-07:00","id":1211818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1211814#post1211814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go with Qualia</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this in principle, but there\u2019s the problem of Qualia having countable plurality, where the other fuel stats are singular mass quantities. You can have less essence, plasm, or glamour, but you would need to have fewer qualia. Instead, I would use the singular \u201cQuale\u201d or the Latin adjective \u201cQualis\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:52:17-07:00","id":1211826,"title":"","content":"I like using &quot;Insight&quot;, personally. In-setting I sometimes use terms stolen from various sources, but that one's both neutral, effective and appropriate, at least if you ask me. And incidentally reminds me of the good times with Bloodborne, which is not a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 04-26-2018, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:45:31-07:00","id":1211888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1211818#post1211818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this in principle, but there\u2019s the problem of Qualia having countable plurality, where the other fuel stats are singular mass quantities. You can have less essence, plasm, or glamour, but you would need to have fewer qualia. Instead, I would use the singular \u201cQuale\u201d or the Latin adjective \u201cQualis\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If that's a problem for anyone, yeah I'd probably go with either &quot;Quale&quot; or &quot;Qualis&quot; as well. I play in Swedish so most things around the table is either translated (which is weird at times), Swenglish or as a loan word if no usable translation is around for a specific term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:36:46-07:00","id":1211911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1211811#post1211811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even for non-malicious Goetia/Dreamborn, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then. To explain my choice: the game series of Schadow Heart works with the classical Goetia Demons of Salomon and there is an power source called malice. <br /> And how I understand goetia demons, they are vorn of sin, failings and denied emotion, so it fits in my opinion. Most of them are malicious other may turn their malice Into good things. I am not realy in the astral planes, so maybe i am wrong about geotia (but i'm open for clarrification if I have a total wrong point of view ^^)<br /> <br /> (English is not my primary language, sorry if my text is a mess)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:49:09-07:00","id":1211915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lykas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1211911#post1211911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then. To explain my choice: the game series of Schadow Heart works with the classical Goetia Demons of Salomon and there is an power source called malice. <br /> And how I understand goetia demons, they are vorn of sin, failings and denied emotion, so it fits in my opinion. Most of them are malicious other may turn their malice Into good things. I am not realy in the astral planes, so maybe i am wrong about geotia (but i'm open for clarrification if I have a total wrong point of view ^^)<br /> <br /> (English is not my primary language, sorry if my text is a mess)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, most goetia aren\u2019t demons, and most aren\u2019t malicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:53:42-07:00","id":1211916,"title":"","content":"How about Musings for the fuel stat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2383-dresden","name":"Dresden","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:30:26-07:00","id":1211935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lykas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1211911#post1211911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even then. To explain my choice: the game series of Schadow Heart works with the classical Goetia Demons of Salomon and there is an power source called malice.<br /> And how I understand goetia demons, they are vorn of sin, failings and denied emotion, so it fits in my opinion. Most of them are malicious other may turn their malice Into good things. I am not realy in the astral planes, so maybe i am wrong about geotia (but i'm open for clarrification if I have a total wrong point of view ^^)<br /> <br /> (English is not my primary language, sorry if my text is a mess)</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be thinking of the Goetic Demons of first edition. Second edition expands this concept into the wider &quot;Goetia&quot;, mind-creatures which represent all sorts of mental constructs, including various &quot;sins&quot; but also stuff like &quot;Jame's love for his brother Thomas&quot; or the abstract concept of &quot;a cowboy&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:44:47-07:00","id":1211939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1211935#post1211935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem to be thinking of the Goetic Demons of first edition. Second edition expands this concept into the wider &quot;Goetia&quot;, mind-creatures which represent all sorts of mental constructs, including various &quot;sins&quot; but also stuff like &quot;Jame's love for his brother Thomas&quot; or the abstract concept of &quot;a cowboy&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or to be clearer: second edition uses &quot;goetia&quot; as synonymous with first edition's &quot;astral entities.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:44:50-07:00","id":1211940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1211935#post1211935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem to be thinking of the Goetic Demons of first edition. Second edition expands this concept into the wider &amp;quot;Goetia&amp;quot;, mind-creatures which represent all sorts of mental constructs, including various &amp;quot;sins&amp;quot; but also stuff like &amp;quot;Jame's love for his brother Thomas&amp;quot; or the abstract concept of &amp;quot;a cowboy&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that was new for me, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T13:14:13-07:00","id":1211952,"title":"","content":"There's a case to be made that if you're going to use &quot;goetia&quot; as a predominantly neutral term it's equally reasonable to use &quot;malice&quot; as a neutral term for such creatures' power...<br /> <br /> That said, &quot;awe&quot;, &quot;focus&quot;, &quot;attention&quot;, or &quot;passion&quot; might serve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:01:17-07:00","id":1211966,"title":"","content":"What about &quot;Intensity&quot;? It covers both the concept of power, and the degree of depth for emotions/feelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:33:27-07:00","id":1211991,"title":"","content":"I guess Libido could work as well, although it has some strong Freudian implications that might be unwanted but it's pretty fitting in the Jungian sense, especially how Jungian the Astral realms are.<br /> Sortal might also be a good choice but i think we're back to the countability problem Charlaquin mentioned beforehand.<br /> Something tells me that Identity could work as well for goetia although it doesn't seem intuitive. Volition I guess seems pretty fitting and Agency seem to work imho.<br /> <br /> The thing though is to find a term usable for all form of astral entities, from the lowly extras in the onerios to the gods of the temenos to the astral planets of the anima mundi and all in between.<br /> Some lack will and goals, working more like machines while others are high concepts with elaborate intelligence beyond our understanding of them<br /> <br /> I'd still go with Qualia (or quale/qualis) though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:24:26-07:00","id":1212745,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would choose 'Pathos'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pathos\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pathos\" target=\"_blank\"> Pathos - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pathos\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pathos </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T15:11:52-07:00","id":1213194,"title":"","content":"&quot;Impetus&quot; could also work. It's both the name of a kinetic force (which makes it rather fitting for an energy meter), and a synonym for a psychological or sociological impulsion or driving force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 04-29-2018, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T22:29:25-07:00","id":1213677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1211826#post1211826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like using &quot;Insight&quot;, personally. In-setting I sometimes use terms stolen from various sources, but that one's both neutral, effective and appropriate, at least if you ask me. And incidentally reminds me of the good times with Bloodborne, which is not a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this I can get behind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11057-sufferian","name":"sufferian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T00:06:26-07:00","id":1213685,"title":"","content":"For my two cents, what do you think of 'pneuma'? It's Greek for 'breath', and is used synonymously with 'soul' or 'spirit'.<br /> <br /> Another option is 'ruach', Hebrew for much the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T04:44:06-07:00","id":1214109,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your suggestions, everyone! There's a lot of great ideas here, and I'm honestly not sure what to go for xD<br /> <br /> For the goetia themselves, I honestly think I'll just fall back on the ol' &quot;astral beings,&quot; unless I want to bump up the word-connection and call them &quot;sidereals.&quot; But I'll definitely put in &quot;dreamborn&quot; as an alternative term, used by certain traditions and cults.<br /> <br /> For the fuel, while I like the varieties on common, appropriate words (&quot;awe&quot; and &quot;insight&quot;, etc.), I'm afraid it'll get confusing while speaking about it. Most other in-game terms have the benefit of being distinctly different from regular discourse (&quot;essence,&quot; ironically, being perhaps the one word that's most likely to be used generally). So, right now, I'm leaning towards &quot;pneuma,&quot; both for ease of use and historical context (and something magi could have used for a really long time) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Again, thanks to everyone for your suggestions! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24057-malus-black","name":"Malus Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T19:29:50-07:00","id":1214397,"title":"","content":"FIGMENTS IS MY SUGGESTION.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T22:02:59-07:00","id":1390193,"title":"","content":"Actually, they use essence too. Ghosts use essence as well. Plasm composes a ghost's ephemera and is created when they expend essence. The horrors of Beasts previously used essence before the Devouring and will use it again after becoming Unfettered. There is even a merit where a horror developes an essence pool alongside a living Beast's Satiety pool. Essence is just the general fuel for ephemeral entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T23:14:43-07:00","id":1390211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1390193#post1390193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, they use essence too. Ghosts use essence as well. Plasm composes a ghost's ephemera and is created when they expend essence. The horrors of Beasts previously used essence before the Devouring and will use it again after becoming Unfettered. There is even a merit where a horror developes an essence pool alongside a living Beast's Satiety pool. Essence is just the general fuel for ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously. Essence is a catch all term for ephemeral fuel. What's being asked about is the feelings and themes evoked by the fuels of the separate ephemeral types. Ghosts are fueled by spooky shit, spirits are fueled by thingness, so it was asked, what fuels goetia? Sure, it's Essence, but what does that mean to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T02:05:02-07:00","id":1390227,"title":"","content":"Aren't Goetia fuelled by &quot;thingness&quot; in a similar way?<br /> <br /> I like Pneuma though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T02:09:13-07:00","id":1390228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1390227#post1390227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't Goetia fuelled by &quot;thingness&quot; in a similar way?<br /> <br /> I like Pneuma though</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its already used, its the premana stuff newly awakened mages have and its also the reason why Archmasters win clashes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T02:35:11-07:00","id":1390234,"title":"","content":"Animus. Not directly the Jungian concept (though the association helps connote a feel), but the vital intent and motive that <i>animates</i> living beings, as derived from Latin associations with breath and the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T03:38:17-07:00","id":1390243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1390193#post1390193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, they use essence too. Ghosts use essence as well. Plasm composes a ghost's ephemera and is created when they expend essence. The horrors of Beasts previously used essence before the Devouring and will use it again after becoming Unfettered. There is even a merit where a horror developes an essence pool alongside a living Beast's Satiety pool. Essence is just the general fuel for ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of the thread is to find an alternative to Essence in a bid to have separate fuel traits for each type of ephemeral being. Everyone here is well aware that both ghosts and goetia use Essence, and ghosts using Plasm is OPs house rule. (Also, a ghost's ephemera/Corpus isn't composed of Plasm; Plasm is actually a waste product from ghosts using Essence and when materialising.)<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1211787-essence-equivalent-for-goetia?p=1390234#post1390234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animus. Not directly the Jungian concept (though the association helps connote a feel), but the vital intent and motive that <i>animates</i> living beings, as derived from Latin associations with breath and the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. It would also provide a nice connection to/duality with Anima Mundi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-20-2020, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T18:25:01-07:00","id":1391376,"title":"","content":"As a casual thought with Implications:<br /> <br /> How about Satiety?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}